WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.200
Michael asks "How do you define Hustle?"

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.320
Michael, this if funny because -- show his face, because I can see him grinning

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.160
This was the first question -- what are we thirty five (35) in? This if the first question in one hundred fifteen (115) questions

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.100
that I can see from the corner of my --
he literally said "How do you define hustle?"

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.860
(laughs)

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.380
Cause you know

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.920
This is a challenging question... so first of all, it's different for everybody, right?

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.220
But what I would say hustle is to me, is that when you have passion around something

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:35.790
that you are squeezing every last bit of the juice out of the orange -- right?!

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.120
To me, hustle is maximizing the energy you're putting in to somebody.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.360
I'm blown away by people saying that they are hustling and they want to achieve these great things,

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.160
and then their actions don't match. It's like saying "You really want to lose weight", while eating a Big Mac, right?

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:57.680
So to me, hustle would be putting all your effort into achieving the goal at hand,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:01.560
and for me that means making every. minute. count.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:08.760
Hiring a full time assistant who is, I mean -- Friday night didn't happen... because I was hustling. Every. Minute.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.440
If i've missed my fifteen (15) minutes to tape this show, i've missed my fifteen (15) minutes, because

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:20.490
there is so much hustle in my day, there is no hanging out. There is no time.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.720
If I get to do one joke with you guys as I am walking in between meetings, you find that to be a rare

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.720
acquaintance  situation. *Occurrence, not acquaintance*

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:34.829
Hustle is putting it all on the line. Hustle is waking up one day the day before you die, and realizing

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:40.520
you gave it your all, into the parenting of your children, the building of your businesses, the philanthropy that

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:45.080
you wanted to do - what ever you define, it's just.. ya know.. "All In"

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:50.000
emotionally and execution-ally. 
In theory, in strategy and in execution.

